    title: "Music: Gear addiction - a reflection",
    body: "I've spent way too much money on guitar gear over the years. The fantasy: new pedal or amp will change how I sound, inspire new songs, solve my tone problems. The reality: I have maybe 20% of my gear even plugged in. The best-sounding tones I've ever made came with two humble pieces of equipment, not because they're objectively the best but because I spent months learning every control intimately. Each new piece of gear requires time to learn, and that's time not spent playing. The gear companies know this - they market to the insecure part of the musician's brain that believes external equipment can substitute for practice and creativity. That said, I'm keeping my two favorite pedals and selling the rest. The minimalist approach feels better.",
