    body: "Sleep gotten worse over past month. Waking up at 3-4am consistently. Ruled out the usual: caffeine intake is stable, room temp is fine, no new stress. Realized the issue might be my magnesium intake dropped when I stopped taking supplements. Started taking magnesium glycinate before bed (glycine also promotes sleep) and sleep improved immediately. Also reading about sleep pressure and circadian rhythm alignment - seems like I've been going to bed too early (fighting sleep pressure), which fragments the night. Pushing bedtime 30 minutes later has helped. The funny thing: the 'right' amount of sleep varies for everyone and shifts seasonally. My winter sleep is longer than my summer sleep, and that's normal.",
