    body: "Legacy code had all styles in one global CSS file. Different pages were overriding each other's styles unpredictably. Started migrating to CSS modules - each component file gets its own .module.css file with local scope by default. Benefits: no naming conflicts, can delete styles without fear of breaking something unseen, easier to refactor. Downside: lose the ability to do site-wide style changes easily. Working through the edge cases now - some shared styles are better in a global utility file. Finding the right balance between modularity and shared style reuse.",
