    body: "Finished Cixin Liu's sci-fi epic. The technological and sociological scope is vast - spans centuries, civilizations, physics. The concept of 'sophons' (dark matter computing elements) that can freeze and unfreeze particle interactions is mind-bending. What struck me most was how the series explores the communication problem: how do you negotiate with an alien civilization if you fundamentally can't trust each other, and each side might have incompatible survival needs? The book is bleak in its assessment of human nature (the Cultural Revolution section especially) but also shows how humans stumble forward anyway. Very different from Western sci-fi which tends toward more optimistic endings.",
