    title: "Work incident - handling customer complaint",
    body: "Customer upset about feature removal. They'd built a workflow around the feature, now it's gone and they're scrambling. I listened to their frustration without immediately defending the product decision. Key insight: I wanted to explain 'why' we removed it (maintenance burden, low usage), but they didn't care about our reasons yet - they cared about the impact on them. Once I acknowledged the impact and asked what they needed instead, conversation shifted from adversarial to collaborative. Ended up finding a workaround and offering transition time. Lesson: empathy first, explanation second. Took 20 minutes instead of the 5 minutes I initially budgeted but resulted in a satisfied customer instead of escalation.",
